codex
The proof is non-vacuous and body-sensitive: an extra-`"!"` postcondition built cleanly and failed with the expected implication residual, and a mutated executed constructor body changed `(12,1)` to `"12"` and made the `"21"` claim fail. Static review found no opaque oracle or proof-local shortcut. It did find a second real-program boundary: the unguarded `pyStr(VInt(I)) => VString(Int2String(I))` rule returns a 4,301-digit string where this CPython 3.10 runtime and both Python implementations raise `ValueError`; the symbolic theorem nevertheless quantifies over that integer.
apply patch
